- Ability row cleanup (Lateralus 13:14/13:2x "the only new rows we should have created are for unique combinations of abilities"; "favors getting rid of our new rows and keeping the identical vanilla row"): section 9. Every FA ability row whose values (Id and Name aside) equal another row is relinked (UnitAbilities + option Ability1/2/3Id) to the lowest-id vanilla row with those values, else the lowest-id FA row; unlinked FA rows are removed. FA rows 380 -> 65 (313 merged, 160 of them into vanilla rows; 2 unused unique rows removed); every kept FA row is unique and none equals a vanilla row. 4 duplicate same-unit links dropped (BMP-3 3, EA-6B 377, ZBD-04 1075 x2). lateralus/china_sf_recon.py check() now checks by unit, not by ability row. Verified: every unit's distinct ability values and every option's slot values unchanged (in-script + independent compare of dev.4 data with/without the cleanup); audit_mp_equipment, check_slot_weapons, audit_swap_prices, check_mount_weapons, check_field_types and queued_checks pass on a test package. MANPAD prices, smoke-off and 8->6 ammo re-asserted after the cleanup. No gameplay change.
- Build check (Lateralus 13:2x "only create new rows when we ask for a unique combination of abilities" / "that also goes for when we are making new units"): lateralus/queued_checks.py fails a 0.9.1-dev.4+ package when an FA ability row has the same values as another row.
